<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 550 0 R
/E (Assessment is a routine part of teaching. After each test, quiz or assignment, a teacher records the marks obtained by every student, compares them with the maximum marks of the assessment and uses the results to decide which students or topics need more attention. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
884 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 550 0 R
/E (In many classrooms these records are maintained in notebooks, spreadsheets or separate files for each subject or assessment. Student details, subject lists, topic lists and marks are therefore stored in different places. Converting marks into percentages, checking which students scored below an expected level and preparing a summary for a class all require repeated manual effort. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
885 0 obj
<<
