<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 552 0 R
/E (The application is accessed through a web browser on the Zoho Creator platform by the teacher, who is also the application owner in the current version. Access through the Zoho Creator mobile app and a customer portal is not part of the current scope. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
917 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 552 0 R
/E (Out of scope. StudyLens does not automatically diagnose the reasons for poor academic performance. It does not use a trained machine learning model, predict future grades or provide personalised AI-generated teaching plans, and it does not integrate with any external system. Features that are not implemented are documented as future enhancements in Section 9.2. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
918 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 552 0 R
/E (A low-code platform lets developers build applications mainly by configuring visual models of data, user interfaces and logic, with hand-written code needed only for specific requirements [1]. Zoho Creator provides a visual form builder, automatically generated reports, a page builder for dashboards and a hosted cloud environment, with the Deluge scripting language available when custom logic is required [2]. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
919 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 552 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
920 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 552 0 R
/E (Using Zoho Creator therefore reduces the amount of conventional code to be written, removes the need to set up a server or database, and makes it easier to add or change fields later. A low-code platform does not remove the need for careful design: correct data modelling, validation of entered marks, testing and access control still have to be planned and verified by the developer. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
