931 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 554 0 R
/E (In a conventional approach, student information, subject details, topic lists and assessment marks are commonly maintained in separate spreadsheets or paper records. The teacher writes or types student details, keeps subject and topic lists in separate files, enters marks for each assessment in a different sheet, calculates percentages manually, and then scans the records to find students who scored below an expected level before preparing any summary by hand. Figure 2.1 shows this general as-is process. It describes the general limitations of manual record keeping and is not a claim about the exact process followed at any particular institution. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [6]
>>
