/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 556 0 R
/T (The sources reviewed fall into two groups. The first group consists of studies of low- code development platforms [1], [3], [4] and the official Zoho Creator documentation, which inform how StudyLens is built. The second group consists of educational research on classroom assessment [5] and learning analytics [6], which provides general background on why recorded assessment results are worth analysing. Table 2.2 summarises these sources. The educational sources are background only: StudyLens implements a simple percentage-threshold rule and does not implement the methods discussed in them. )
/E (The sources reviewed fall into two groups. The first group consists of studies of low- code development platforms [1], [3], [4] and the official Zoho Creator documentation, which inform how StudyLens is built. The second group consists of educational research on classroom assessment [5] and learning analytics [6], which provides general background on why recorded assessment results are worth analysing. Table 2.2 summarises these sources. The educational sources are background only: StudyLens implements a simple percentage-threshold rule and does not implement the methods discussed in them. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [29]
>>
