1052 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 558 0 R
/E (Citizen development. Low-code tools allow people with domain knowledge but limited programming experience to build simple applications. StudyLens reflects this trend: its structure \(students, subjects, topics, assessments\) mirrors how a teacher already thinks about assessment records, so it can be understood and modified without deep programming knowledge. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1053 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 558 0 R
/E (Convergence with model-driven engineering. Low-code development is closely related to model-driven engineering, in which models are the main development artefacts [4]. In StudyLens, the form definitions act as the model from which the platform generates storage and user interface. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
