1492 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 570 0 R
/E (StudyLens was created from scratch as a new application in the Zoho Creator account of the developer using the visual Form Builder and Page Builder. The application is organised into six navigation sections that correspond to its modules: Dashboard, Students, Subjects, Topics, Assessments and Learning Gap Analysis \(Figure 4.4\). A clean purple-and-white theme with readable labels was chosen to keep the interface simple for a teacher \(Figure 5.1\). )
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1493 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 570 0 R
/T (5.2 Forms and Data Capture )
/E (5.2 Forms and Data Capture )
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1494 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 570 0 R
/E (StudyLens uses four forms, designed as specified in Tables 4.2 to 4.5. Each submitted form creates a record in the application database, which then appears in the corresponding report. )
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1495 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 570 0 R
/E (Students form. Captures Student Name, Email and Course. Using the Email field type allows the platform to check that the entered value is in a valid email format. )
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1496 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 570 0 R
/E (Subjects form. Stores the name of each subject, such as Mathematics, Python Programming or Database Management \(sample data\). )
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1497 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 570 0 R
/E (Topics form. Stores the Topic Name, the Subject Name to which the topic belongs and a Difficulty Level chosen from Easy, Medium or Hard. Organising topics under subjects allows assessment records to be grouped by learning area. )
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
